DISPOSITION

The engineering work is done and it is good. B1 and F5 were fixed properly —
the right relation, in the right place, red before green, with regression
tests that assert the refusal and the non-write. `red` still refuses to
record a passing command, files-owned discipline still holds, the suite is
871 green, and verify and `npm test` finally agree. If the question were
"is the code right", this is a pass.

The question is whether W-020 may be recorded `done`, and the answer on the
tree in front of me is no: `check` blocks on this opus's own missing reds,
and the close is what would silence it. Round 1 closed this opus on the
builder's own say-so. I am not closing it on a rule's blind spot.

W-020 stays in `building`. It needs a Patron decision on behaviours 9-11's
reds — waive on the record, or leave the opus open — and then a round 4 that
is one line long.

Recorded with `bisellium review W-020 --fail --evidence ci/W-020-review-3.log
